## 2026-11-18 — Premium P20 complete
- "Where the yield went" per premium §7.9 + §11.3. The Pareto is now a `surface` section card (`r-2xl`, `shadow-card`, padding 24 / 16 mobile) with a `title-2` title, the bin-type segmented control on the right, the takeaway "One bin holds 91.3% of the lost dies.", the lot yield loss as one `stat-s` number, and the "Yield loss by bin" / "Share of all dies" labels. Rows are 40 px `88px 1fr 56px 88px 56px` grids (`r-md`, hover `fill-1`, pressed `fill-2` at 0.985). Each row has the code (bin name in a 600 ms tooltip), an 8 px `r-xs` bar scaled to the largest share, share of all dies, die count, and a share-of-fails pill (`caption`, `fill-2`, pill). The top-loss bin is the only solid `ember-mark` bar; the others are `bar-neutral` at 40 % with a 1 px `hairline-strong` outline. A selected row (clicked or linked) gets `fill-2` and `aria-pressed`, and a selected non-dominant bar turns `ink` (dark `text-primary`). The track, cumulative tick, and detail line are gone. The top 6 rows show, then a text button "Show all N bins". The empty line reads "No yield loss. Every die passed." Keys: `pareto.title/takeaway/chartLabel/axisLabel/lossLabel` added, `pareto.heading/rowDetail` removed, `pareto.empty` reworded; 236 keys in all 5 locales.
- Verified: typecheck and lint clean, `pnpm test` 302/302 (50 files). After a fresh build, e2e `pareto-p20` (new, A32 + A43, light and dark, 2/2), `bin-pareto-task10` (updated), `yield-summary-task11`, `findings-p19`, `stats-p18`, `verdict-p17`, `vertical-slice`, `editorial-p26b` (failed once under batch load, passed on rerun), `loaded-desktop-p12`, `loaded-responsive-p13`, and `typography-p4` pass. No snapshot changes.
- Decisions (restrained): §11.3 says to keep the existing segmented control, so the section keeps its own SBIN/HBIN switch and does not follow the stage mode as §7.9 asks. The "one big number" sits on its own line under the takeaway, captioned "Yield lost" (new key `pareto.lossLabel`). The pill shows the share of fails. Its count-up is left to P28. Below a 448 px card width (a container query) the count column hides; it stays in the row's aria-label. The Edge-Ring finding cites no bin, so a claim without a cited bin of the current kind selects the bin holding most of its failing dies (`resolveClaimMatchedBinCode`, UI-only). Ember stays `ember-mark`, as §3.4 says.
